<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's April base metals import prices down.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's April base metals import prices down.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's non-ferrous metals import prices fell in April from the previous month due to losses on the London Metal Exchange (LME), the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Import prices of base metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(price per tonne on CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		     Origin     Apr	 Mar</p>
<p> Copper (99.95 pct)    Chile     2,470     2,500</p>
<p> Copper scrap (berry)  U.S.	2,348     2,513</p>
<p> Aluminium (99.7 pct)  Australia 1,645     1,722</p>
<p> Lead (99.99 pct)	China	 715	 745</p>
<p> Zinc (99.995 pct)     S.America 1,340     1,315</p>
<p> Nickel (99.9 pct)     Canada    7,574     8,150</p>
<p> Tin (99.85 pct)	 Malaysia  5,761     5,840</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
